{{!-- The stat block: stats, the three debilities, and the vitals row (damage / HP /
      armor / XP / level).

      It heads the Moves tab. It used to sit above the tabs, always on screen, which cost
      every other page the same ~200px of header before a single item was visible; it is
      one page's header now, and the page it belongs to is the one a player rolls from.
      What stays pinned above the tabs is the portrait, playbook, name and appearance —
      plus the wounds line, which is a live harm track a player needs to see whatever page
      they are reading.

      The `.sheet-top` wrapper is kept despite no longer being the top of anything:
      pbta's own stylesheet skins this block through `.pbta.sheet .sheet-wrapper
      .sheet-top .sheet-attributes-top …` chains (and our 2:1 vitals-width rule matches
      that specificity deliberately), so dropping the class would silently unstyle the
      vitals row. Descendant selectors, so they still resolve from inside the tab. --}}
<section class="sheet-top flexcol">
	<div class="stonetop-details-heading-row">
		{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.character.stats.sectionTitle") note=stonetop.statsNoteDisplay}}
		{{> "stonetop.details-section-edit-toggle" section="stats" editing=stonetop.statsEdit collapse="stats"}}
	</div>

	<section class="sheet-attributes flexrow">
		{{> "stonetop.actor-stats"}}
	</section>
	{{!-- The three debilities. While the Heavy is in their Battle Joy they stay TICKED and stop
	      doing anything — "you ignore fear, pain, mind-control, and the effects of debilities as
	      long as you keep fighting" — so the block goes grey rather than the boxes clearing. The
	      distinction matters: the debilities are still marked, and will bite again the moment the
	      action stops. The roll path reads the same state (StonetopCharacter#ignoresDebilities), so
	      what this says and what the dice do cannot disagree. --}}
	<div class="stonetop-debilities{{#if stonetop.battleJoy.raging}} is-ignored{{/if}}"
	     {{#if stonetop.battleJoy.raging}}data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.battleJoy.debilitiesIgnored"}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP"{{/if}}>
		<div class="stonetop-debility">
			<span class="stonetop-debility-bracket"></span>
			<label class="stonetop-debility-control" data-tooltip="Fatigued, tired, sluggish, shaky. Disadvantage on +STR or +DEX rolls." data-tooltip-direction="UP">
				<input type="checkbox" class="attr-list"
				       name="system.attributes.debilities.options.weakened.value"
				       {{#if system.attributes.debilities.options.weakened.value}}checked{{/if}}>
				<span class="stonetop-debility-label">weakened</span>
			</label>
		</div>
		<div class="stonetop-debility">
			<span class="stonetop-debility-bracket"></span>
			<label class="stonetop-debility-control" data-tooltip="Out of it, befuddled, not thinking clearly. Disadvantage on +INT or +WIS rolls." data-tooltip-direction="UP">
				<input type="checkbox" class="attr-list"
				       name="system.attributes.debilities.options.dazed.value"
				       {{#if system.attributes.debilities.options.dazed.value}}checked{{/if}}>
				<span class="stonetop-debility-label">dazed</span>
			</label>
		</div>
		<div class="stonetop-debility">
			<span class="stonetop-debility-bracket"></span>
			<label class="stonetop-debility-control" data-tooltip="Greatly distressed, angry, unwell, in pain. Disadvantage on +CON or +CHA rolls." data-tooltip-direction="UP">
				<input type="checkbox" class="attr-list"
				       name="system.attributes.debilities.options.miserable.value"
				       {{#if system.attributes.debilities.options.miserable.value}}checked{{/if}}>
				<span class="stonetop-debility-label">miserable</span>
			</label>
		</div>
	</div>

	<section class="sheet-attributes-top">
		{{> "stonetop.actor-vitals"}}
	</section>
</section>
